      "story_id": 1,
      "headline": "Carney secures Liberal majority via byelection sweep and floor crossings",
      "summary": "Prime Minister Mark Carney's Liberals secured a majority in the House of Commons on April 13 by winning all three byelections (Scarborough Southwest, University\u2013Rosedale, Terrebonne) and absorbing five floor-crossers from the Conservatives and NDP, pushing the party to 174 seats. The Terrebonne contest against the Bloc Qu\u00e9b\u00e9cois was closely watched; Liberal candidate Tatiana Auguste won her second consecutive race in the former sovereigntist stronghold. Opposition parties, particularly Conservatives, challenged the majority's legitimacy, calling floor crossings 'backroom deals.'",
